# Netlify redirect / access rules
#
# The publish directory IS the repository root (netlify.toml: publish = "."), so
# repository-only files would otherwise be readable over HTTP. They are not part of
# the website and must not be served.
#
# The trailing '!' on the STATUS CODE is required to force the rule past an existing
# static file. Netlify's shadowing behaviour means a redirect is otherwise ignored
# whenever a file matches the path. Syntax documented at
# docs.netlify.com/manage/routing/redirects/redirect-options#force-redirects
#
# /content/site.json is deliberately NOT blocked: main.js fetches it at runtime for
# the header and footer. /admin/* is the CMS and stays reachable.

# repository documentation - the file describing a different business
/readme.md               /404-not-found  404!

# same file, upper-case path
/README.md               /404-not-found  404!

# build toolchain: generator, templates, notes
/build/*                 /404-not-found  404!

# git internals
/.git/*                  /404-not-found  404!

# git config file
/.gitattributes          /404-not-found  404!

# git config file
/.gitignore              /404-not-found  404!

# content source only the build needs (site.json stays reachable)
/content/policies.json   /404-not-found  404!

# TEMPORARY - the CMS is closed until Identity registration is invite-only.
#
# Why: registration is currently OPEN (Identity disable_signup = false) and Git
# Gateway has no Roles restriction, so "any logged in user" means "anyone who
# registers". Anyone who found this path could create an account and edit the
# live site, committing through the gateway into the repo.
#
# REMOVE THIS RULE once Identity -> Settings -> Registration is set to
# "Invite only" (the detail on the rule's status code matters: Netlify only
# applies a redirect over an existing static file when forced with 404!).
/admin/*                 /404-not-found  404!
